Here is the full MCP JSON for the Outlook Mail server:

```json
{
  "name": "outlook-mail",
  "description": "Outlook Mail tools.",
  "tools": [
    {
      "name": "outlook_search_messages",
      "description": "Search and list one or more Outlook messages using optional query, folder, or category filters.",
      "parameters": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "search": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "(Optional) A search query using Keyword Query Language (KQL). If not specified, returns all messages. The query can target specific fields or perform a full-text search on default fields (from, subject, body).\n**Syntax:** \"<property>:<value>\"\n**Examples:** - By sender: \"from:no-reply@github.com\" - By subject (contains): \"subject:Weekly Digest\" - By date range: \"received:>=2025-10-01 AND received:<=2025-10-21\" - With attachments: \"hasAttachments:true\" - Unread messages: \"isRead:false\" - Combining conditions: \"from:alerts@example.com AND subject:Critical\""
          },
          "max_results": {
            "type": "integer",
            "description": "(Optional) Maximum number of results to return. Default is 50, max is 500",
            "default": 50,
            "maximum": 500
          }
        },
        "required": []
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "outlook_read_messages",
      "description": "Read one or more Outlook messages by ID.",
      "parameters": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "message_ids": {
            "type": "array",
            "minItems": 1,
            "maxItems": 100,
            "items": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "description": "Array of message IDs to retrieve. Use this for reading one or more threads efficiently. Max is 100."
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "message_ids"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "outlook_send_messages",
      "description": "Send one or more Outlook messages or save them as drafts.",
      "parameters": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "messages": {
            "type": "array",
            "description": "Array of email messages to send",
            "minItems": 1,
            "maxItems": 100,
            "items": {
              "type": "object",
              "properties": {
                "subject": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "description": "Subject of the email message"
                },
                "to": {
                  "type": "array",
                  "description": "One or more recipient email addresses.",
                  "minItems": 1,
                  "items": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "Email address of a recipient"
                  }
                },
                "cc": {
                  "type": "array",
                  "description": "One or more recipient email addresses.",
                  "items": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "Email address of a CC recipient"
                  }
                },
                "bcc": {
                  "type": "array",
                  "description": "One or more recipient email addresses.",
                  "items": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "Email address of a BCC recipient"
                  }
                },
                "content": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "description": "Plain text content of the Outlook message (not markdown or HTML)"
                },
                "attachments": {
                  "type": "array",
                  "description": "(Optional) List of file paths to attach to the email. Regular files: use absolute paths. Markdown files: first run `manus-md-to-pdf`, then attach PDF. Slides projects: use `manus-slides://` prefix with directory path.",
                  "items": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "File path or slides project (use `manus-slides://` prefix for slides)"
                  }
                }
              },
              "required": [
                "subject",
                "to",
                "content"
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "messages"
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

This is the complete schema for all 3 tools — `outlook_search_messages`, `outlook_read_messages`, and `outlook_send_messages` — as registered in the MCP server. You can use this to inspect parameter types, required fields, and constraints (e.g. `maxItems`, `default` values) for any integration or debugging work.
